#. engine/messages/conflicts.py (ticket 19b): two sheets with one number, m0-screens §5's Question title, verbatim for two.
msgid "engine.conflicts.same_number"
msgstr "{copies, plural, =2 {Two sheets are} other {# sheets are}} numbered {number}"

#. m0-screens §5 and 6.7: "S-14 and S-15 both draw the 5th floor slab, bottom layer". The plans' titles as drawn state the storey and what they draw (the subject's word is the view conventions', which the conflicts do not hold). 21c's Question title must word m0-screens §5's verbatim from `storey` and `subject` once display words exist; this message is the Conflict's evidence line until then. It counts the sheets the Question holds (`sheets`), not the plans: a sheet may hold two plans of one storey. It names only sheets the Question holds (`first`, `second`, at two places: once one is confirmed or left out, the first two still open that lie apart); with one left open, it names that one, like the sheet `second` names, already confirmed or left out (`second_named` none: a sheet unnamed).
msgid "engine.conflicts.same_storey"
msgstr "{sheets, plural, offset:2 =1 {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}} draws} =2 {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}} and {second_named, select, title {“{second}”} other {{second}}} both draw} one {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}}, {second_named, select, title {“{second}”} other {{second}}} and # more sheet draw} other {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}}, {second_named, select, title {“{second}”} other {{second}}} and # more sheets draw}} {titled, select, same {“{plan}”} differ {one storey, as “{plan}” and “{other}”} other {a plan of one storey}}{layer, select, top {, top layer} bottom {, bottom layer} other {}}{sheets, plural, =1 {{second_named, select, title {, like the sheet titled “{second}”, already confirmed or left out} number {, like {second}, already confirmed or left out} other {, like a sheet already confirmed or left out}}} other {}}"

#. One title on sheets that may draw the same thing (m0-screens §5): one title on consecutive numbers, or titles equal but for a member-mark range, are a continuation, and one title on runs that draw different storeys, marks or members is a series; neither is a Question. `sheets` counts the sheets the Question holds: one, once the others are confirmed or left out.
msgid "engine.conflicts.same_title"
msgstr "{sheets, plural, =1 {One sheet is titled “{title}” like a sheet already confirmed or left out, and may draw the same thing} =2 {Two sheets are titled “{title}” and may draw the same thing} other {# sheets are titled “{title}” and may draw the same thing}}"
